WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.583
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.583 --> 00:00:10.133
Working for a development finance
institution at the forefront of poverty

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:11.649
mediation in Cameroon,

00:00:11.649 --> 00:00:15.920
I had the amazing opportunity to move to
Cote d'Ivoire as an analyst.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.230
I was excited, not just because Côte
d'Ivoire was the largest economy in French

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.730
speaking west Africa, but because Côte
d'Ivoire was preparing for elections which

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:31.040
was expected to mark the beginning of a
new era, and I wanted to be part of this.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:36.860
Barely two weeks after I officially moved
to Côte d'Ivoire in [INAUDIBLE],

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:37.780
I was asked to leave.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.210
Why?

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.850
The political situation had deteriorated
so rapidly.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.830
The elections did not have the desired
results.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:54.430
I moved to Senegal to work for the same
company and I started liking the place.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.835
Fast forward six months.

00:00:55.835 --> 00:00:57.560
&gt;&gt; [COUGH]
&gt;&gt; I had settled in and

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.790
I started forming new rituals.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:04.560
One of them was sitting at a cafe on
Sunday afternoon,

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.540
sipping a hot cup of green tea, pondering
over the week ahead of me,

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.970
often distracted by the waves as they hit
the shore.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.210
But this particular Sunday was different.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.390
I had a very difficult decision to make.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.970
A political resolution to the civil war in
Côte d'Ivoire had been reached and

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:30.080
I was asked to go back, but the security
situation had not improved significantly.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:36.917
Burned buildings, displaced family, a
heightened sence of uncertainty.

00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:39.292
[BLANK_AUDIO]

00:01:39.292 --> 00:01:43.760
Cote d'Ivoire once known as the Paris of
Africa was a shadow of its former self.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.920
I had a difficult decision to make that
day.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:54.050
And the decision was between staying in
Senegal or going back to Côte d’Ivoire.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.835
Of course, I was going to stay in Senegal.

00:01:55.835 --> 00:01:58.690
[LAUGH].

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:02.821
I informed my boss that I was going to
stay in Senegal, but

00:02:02.821 --> 00:02:05.417
she told me to think about it again.

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:08.519
Between war torn Côte d’Ivoire and
peaceful Senegal,

00:02:08.519 --> 00:02:10.500
what else was there to think about?

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.125
[LAUGH].

00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:16.063
But then, given I had more time in my
hands to think about it,

00:02:16.063 --> 00:02:19.590
this forced me to look at the situation
differently.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:24.190
I had spent all my time focusing on the
advantages of staying in Senegal and

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.230
the disadvantages of going back to Côte
d’Ivoire.

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:31.495
I had not even bothered to look at the
advantages of staying in Côte d'Ivoire and

00:02:31.495 --> 00:02:34.333
the disadvantages of staying in Senegal.

00:02:34.333 --> 00:02:38.458
[BLANK_AUDIO]

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:42.806
Often times in life we miss the beauty in
the unattractive because we,

00:02:42.806 --> 00:02:47.210
we spend so much time focusing on that
attractive option.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.960
I had to take a step back and

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.530
realize the decision was not just between
a war torn country and a peaceful country.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:56.240
The decision was between saving myself
versus

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.958
missing an opportunity to help other
people.

00:02:58.958 --> 00:03:05.833
[BLANK_AUDIO]

00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:09.913
There is an important variable in decision
making that we often times miss because we

00:03:09.913 --> 00:03:11.700
do not look underneath the surface.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:17.500
And this important variable is staying
true to who we are, authenticity.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:23.530
The degree to which one is aligned with
one's own person, personality,

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:27.610
character, despite all the external
pressures defines authenticity.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.640
Authenticity does not just apply to my
decision to go back to Côte d’Ivoire,

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.100
it also applies in business and leadership
as well.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:41.146
At the GSB, we are taught cost benefit
analysis.

00:03:41.146 --> 00:03:45.490
Quantify all the costs, quantify all the
revenues, and decide whether or

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:46.790
not to proceed with the project.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.560
But sometimes, we must realize that a
project's costs may exceed the revenues,

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.460
but then be so aligned with who we are as
a person and, therefore, worth pursuing.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:00.300
On the other hand, a project will be
profitable, but

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.570
not worth pursuing because it doesn't
align with who we are as a person.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:12.780
Given for example, when Disney decided to
acquire Pixar,

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.790
some people said this was not worth it.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.540
Why should Disney acquire an animation
company at such a huge financial cost?

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.970
They could develop animation internally.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.930
But then Disney realized that
entertainment,

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:29.880
entertaining people was its core value,
and animation was an important variable,

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.420
and therefore it was worth pursuing even
though it was a huge financial cost.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:39.020
On the other hand we know the AOL Time
Warner measure.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.460
On paper the numbers look great.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:45.570
It was even once hailed as the marriage of
the old and new media.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:49.999
But culture mismanaged an important
variable was heating below the surface.

00:04:49.999 --> 00:04:52.958
[BLANK_AUDIO]

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:56.210
Today authentic leadership is gaining
momentum.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:01.140
They Harvard Business Review defines
authentic leadership

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:04.790
as the courageous pursuit of one's self
awareness.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:09.290
You will be surprised to find out when

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:12.550
some of the five members of the Standford
Graduate Business School

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:17.770
advisory council were asked one important
leadership trait leaders should develop.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:21.710
Your answer was almost unanimous, self
awareness.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:26.650
Knowing who you truly are, there are so

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:30.780
many advantages of knowing who we truly
are.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.770
Carl Jung, the father of analytical
psychology summarizes this advantages

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:41.010
well, when he says that the true privilege
of a lifetime is knowing who you are.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.960
How many times have you made a decision
and

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.110
then when you dug underneath the surface,
you were surprised to find out that

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:53.880
the option you thought was the best was
not the best option.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:59.210
The unattractive alternative which you had
dismissed at the beginning

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.985
ended up being the best solution for the
problem you were looking at.

00:06:01.985 --> 00:06:04.351
I certainly have.

00:06:04.351 --> 00:06:07.340
[LAUGH].

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.620
When deciding to go back to Cote d'Ivoire
I spent all my time focusing

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.580
on what I thought was attractive.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.720
Staying in a beautiful country.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.800
Observing my rituals on Sunday afternoons.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:22.390
By then I didn't realize that I had to
look underneath the surface

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:24.580
to realize what I was really choosing
between.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:30.560
Returning to Côte d'Ivoire was one of the
best decisions of my life.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:34.910
I had the amazing opportunity to work on
exciting initiatives,

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.920
I would otherwise not have worked on if I
had stayed in Senegal.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:41.740
I even got the opportunity to chat with
the First Lady of Côte d'Ivoire.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:48.130
Every day in life we make 100s if not
1000s of decisions.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.600
Whether you turn left or right.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.895
Whether you press the snooze button in the
morning.

00:06:52.895 --> 00:06:54.820
[LAUGH].

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:56.245
&gt;&gt; Some of them are pretty easy.

00:06:56.245 --> 00:07:01.550
[LAUGH].

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:06.890
But then once in awhile life chose very
difficult decisions of us,

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:10.990
which can change the course of our lives,
our careers, or even our businesses.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.970
As it was the case for me a few years ago.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:19.610
I want to encourage all of us to look at
all the options we have before us equally.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:24.720
Even those we think are unattractive, and
even impossible.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:28.360
We will find the beauty in the
unattractive, we'd otherwise have missed.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:33.532
The next time you do a cost benefits
analysis of a situation,

00:07:33.532 --> 00:07:36.042
remember it is only part of the picture.

00:07:36.042 --> 00:07:40.762
Do not underestimate the power that total
evaluation of all the alternatives,

00:07:40.762 --> 00:07:42.458
would have in your success.

00:07:42.458 --> 00:07:43.375
Thank you.

00:07:43.375 --> 00:07:45.750
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:49.599
[MUSIC]

